---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import {
  milestones,
  operatorFamilies,
  repositoryUrl,
} from "../data/site";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<SiteLayout active="Overview">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Rust-native GPU kernels</p>
      <h1>The operator layer for LLM inference.</h1>
      <p>
        Loom Infer defines checked Rust contracts, compiles Rust device kernels,
        and is building one execution model for Rust kernels and vendor
        libraries.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}/docs/operators/`}>Operators</a>
        <a class="button" href={repositoryUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">GitHub</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kernel-window" aria-label="Target operator execution path">
      <div class="window-bar">
        <span>one operator lifecycle</span>
        <span class="window-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      </div>
      <pre class="kernel-code"><code><span class="token-keyword">validated spec</span>
  → immutable plan
  → checked bindings
  → enqueue
  → <span class="token-type">Rust kernel | vendor provider</span>

<span class="token-comment">admission target: no tuning, allocation, or fallback in enqueue</span></code></pre>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="metrics-strip" aria-label="Project status">
    <div class="metric"><strong>5</strong><span>qualified device slices</span></div>
    <div class="metric"><strong>SM90</strong><span>first target</span></div>
    <div class="metric"><strong>Rust</strong><span>host and device source</span></div>
    <div class="metric"><strong>Matched</strong><span>first eager performance evidence</span></div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="operators">
    <header class="section-header">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Scope</p>
        <h2>The inference operator surface</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Attention is central. Decode, KV, MoE, quantization, and vendor GEMM
        integration complete the inference path.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="operator-grid">
      {operatorFamilies.map((family, index) => (
        <article class="operator-card">
          <span class="card-index">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
          <h3>{family.name}</h3>
          <p>{family.boundary}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <header class="section-header">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Architecture</p>
        <h2>Rust owns the path</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        CPU references define behavior. Plans fix algorithms and launch
        configurations. Bindings share reads and own writable buffers.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="architecture-grid">
      <article class="architecture-card">
        <span class="card-index">01</span><h3>Contract</h3>
        <p>Shapes, dtypes, layouts, aliasing, and numerical rules.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="architecture-card">
        <span class="card-index">02</span><h3>Plan</h3>
        <p>Provider, tactic, artifact, launch, workspace, and graph policy.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="architecture-card">
        <span class="card-index">03</span><h3>Binding</h3>
        <p>Exact spans, device, context, stream, and access mode.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="architecture-card">
        <span class="card-index">04</span><h3>Execution</h3>
        <p>Rust device artifacts and fixed vendor calls share one checked command scope.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="evidence">
    <header class="section-header">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Evidence</p><h2>Permanent providers only</h2></div>
      <p>Every claim identifies its source, hardware, boundary, and artifact.</p>
    </header>
    <article class="evidence-card">
      <h3>RMSNorm on H20</h3><span class="result">Qualified</span>
      <p>The owned-binding F32, FP16, and BF16 paths pass correctness.</p>
      <small>Memcheck, racecheck, and synccheck report no errors.</small>
    </article>
    <article class="evidence-card">
      <h3>BF16 cuBLASLt GEMM on H20</h3><span class="result">Qualified</span>
      <p>The fixed plan and RMSNorm-to-GEMM Graph pass correctness.</p>
      <small>The final output after two replays is bit-exact. Memcheck reports no errors or leaks.</small>
    </article>
    <article class="evidence-card">
      <h3>BF16 single decode on H20</h3><span class="result">Qualified</span>
      <p>Direct and split-K NHD D128 MHA, MQA, and GQA cases pass.</p>
      <small>Four sanitizer tools report no errors. Parallel merge reduces the recorded KV4096 gap from 80.08x to 2.09x.</small>
    </article>
    <article class="evidence-card">
      <h3>BF16 paged decode on H20</h3><span class="result">Qualified</span>
      <p>NHD D128 page-size-16 MHA, MQA, and GQA batches pass.</p>
      <small>Eight-warp token parallelism puts Loom 4.41x ahead on MHA and 2.35x ahead on matched MQA. GQA ranking remains order-sensitive.</small>
    </article>
    <article class="evidence-card">
      <h3>BF16 ragged prefill on H20</h3><span class="result">Qualified</span>
      <p>Direct and specialized eight/sixteen-warp causal MHA, MQA, and GQA pass.</p>
      <small>Mixed MQA is 7.245x faster than direct and now trails FlashInfer by 1.353x. Long GQA remains 10.028x behind.</small>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <header class="section-header">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Next</p><h2>Extend and profile attention</h2></div>
      <p>Add ragged query tiling and K/V reuse, then qualify fixed-address Graph replay and real model invocation.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="roadmap-grid">
      {milestones.map((item) => (
        <article class="roadmap-card">
          <span class="card-index">{item.milestone}</span>
          <h3>{item.name}</h3><p>{item.reason}</p>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band">
    <div><h2>Start with the boundary</h2><p>Read the architecture before adding a kernel.</p></div>
    <a class="button primary" href={`${base}/docs/`}>Documentation</a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
